Take struct cachestat from the kernel headers rather than declaring it here.

fincore declares the two records itself whenever the C library has no
cachestat() to call. The records are the kernel's, and <linux/mman.h> has
carried them since 6.5; a library whose <sys/mman.h> reaches that header for
its arch specific MAP_ values therefore has them already, and the second
declaration is an error rather than a fallback.

Including the kernel header outright leaves the wrapper below, which is what
was actually missing.

--- a/misc-utils/fincore.c
+++ b/misc-utils/fincore.c
@@ -57,18 +57,7 @@
 #endif
 #endif
 
-struct cachestat_range {
-	uint64_t off;
-	uint64_t len;
-};
-
-struct cachestat {
-	uint64_t nr_cache;
-	uint64_t nr_dirty;
-	uint64_t nr_writeback;
-	uint64_t nr_evicted;
-	uint64_t nr_recently_evicted;
-};
+#include <linux/mman.h>
 
 static inline int cachestat(unsigned int fd,
 			    const struct cachestat_range *cstat_range,
